cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CleanSpeX in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CleanSpeX: a browser-based tool for PlantEye spectral phenotyping data cleaning and exploration"
abstract: "CleanSpeX is a free, browser-based application for cleaning, exploring and exporting spectral phenotyping data acquired with the PlantEye F600 multispectral 3D scanner (Phenospex). It runs entirely in the browser via WebR and shinylive: scans are aggregated to daily means per plant, pots can be excluded from an interactive bench map, and cleaned data can be explored with time-series charts and boxplots and exported in wide or long format."
